<p>Exciting stuff here. : D</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Comments.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Comments.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-2845 is a quadruped entity, measuring 2.9 meters in height at the shoulder and weighing 815 kilograms. A sinuous neck, generally held in an upright position, extends a further .5&#160;m, terminating in a head with humanoid facial features.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The Spirit of the Forest from Princess Mononoke?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A ring of ice particles is suspended 15&#160;cm behind SCP-2845’s skull, measuring 1.7&#160;m in diameter, with a ring thickness of 35&#160;cm. This ring is interrupted at regular intervals by seven spheres consisting of metallic hydrogen and metallic helium, each measuring 15&#160;cm in diameter. The ring and spheres rotate clockwise at a speed of 1.6 rpm.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Budda?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The most common forms of offensive transmutation used by SCP-2845 are a column measuring five to seven meters in diameter and sixty to eighty meters in height, or a horizontal cone measuring between one hundred and one hundred and fifty meters in length and ten to thirty meters in width at the furthest end.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Okay, I admit it, I'm lost here.</p>
<p>So&#8230; it breaks the masquerade. Tragic. Okay, it's a big thing, and it's perhaps too far-reaching for it to be a mainlister and not a tale, yet I honestly don't care about that.</p>
<p>Perhaps what Mr Carbon mentioned earlier (the ending is too sudden, too &quot;hamfisted&quot;) is what bothers me the most, but otherwise? This thing is a perfect representation of an Eldritch God-King arriving into Earth. Were this thing to be a two kilometers-tall titan, it would belong in an NGE standalone movie. It is strange and alien and it shocks our world. I <em>like</em> it.</p>
<p>Thus, even if it many others make valid points in this Discussion page, upvoted. Most other authors will ignore this SCP altogether, and that's fine&#8230; the Foundation canon is broad and diffuse enough as to allow most stuff in it to exist without interacting with most other articles. Although I want to see what changes can be done to it.</p>
<p>Thanks for the good read, whether this survives or not.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Edit: Now that it seems it's here to stay, designated for the SCP-ES translation pool. Really exciting stuff. :_D</p>

